{"name":"Brown Tumbleweed","hex":"#37290e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"},{"term":"tumbleweed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant which habitually breaks away from its roots once dry, forming a light, rolling mass which is driven by the wind from place to place; as Russian thistle, wild indigo, witch grass, Amaranthus albus, etc.","One of the dried-out, seed-dispersing, globular forms of such plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tumbleweed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tumbleweed","blocks":[{"text":"A tumbleweed is any structural part of the above-ground anatomy of a number of species of plants. It is a diaspore that, once mature and dry, detaches from its root or stem and rolls due to the force of the wind. It is also the name used for these types of plants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Tumbleweed_in_motion.webm/330px--Tumbleweed_in_motion.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumbleweed","wikidata":"Q1060486"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Tumbleweed_Blooming.jpg/500px-Tumbleweed_Blooming.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai